# Fixed defect 133, 2026-09-29, the shapes beside it. Symptom of the repair
# refused: the parser reading every certain swap as the keyword it writes,
# as a lexer emitting `function` for `fn` would, cost a second diagnostic
# wherever the swap is wrong where the word stands, each quoting a word the
# author never wrote: `function fn(` cost `expected_name` "found
# `function`", `record struct` cost `continuation_outside_brackets` and
# `expected_name`, and `const x = 5` in a body cost `expected_expression`,
# measured on 2026-09-29. Cause: a keyword stands where the grammar expects
# it and nowhere else. So the parser reads a swap only where it dispatches
# on the keyword the swap writes (`parse/swap_reading.hero`), and each line
# below costs its `reserved_word` alone. That the certain fix writes a new
# error in these three places is defect 015's class, not this one's.
#
# Widened the same day: a swapped word on a head's OWN line is junk the
# lexer has reported, and that report is the one message. The guards that
# read the next line's head as its swap read it there too, so `function
# show() fn` over a body cost `missing_body` "found `fn`" beside the
# `reserved_word`, `record Pair fn` over fields and `variant Kind struct`
# over cases each a second message, and `extern "m.h" fn` read the `fn` as a
# declaration with no name. The swap is now read only where the word opens
# its line (`swap_reading.opens_line_as`), and each of these costs its
# `reserved_word` alone; the certain fix writes a keyword where none can
# stand, which is defect 015's class again.
#
# Repaired the same day, a second round: a swap is `certain` only where the
# word it writes is right where it stands (`foreign_at.hero`,
# `word_place.hero`), so none of the six lines below offers one any more,
# and each message says what is right there: a name that cannot be the
# word, a value bound with `=`, a word that has no place on its line.
# `--apply` writes the file back unchanged.

function fn(x: i64) -> i64  #~ reserved_word
    return x

record struct  #~ reserved_word
    x: i64

function main()
    const x = 5  #~ reserved_word
    print(x)

function show() fn  #~ reserved_word
    print(1)

record Pair fn  #~ reserved_word
    x: i64

variant Kind struct  #~ reserved_word
    a
